{"seconds": 54.9, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! The move is **Bxf3**. After this move, White's Bg5 is hanging to the queen, and any recapture allows Black to take the bishop with Qxg5, winning material decisively. The key idea is that by removing the Nf3 defender, Black exposes the Bg5 to capture by the queen along the long diagonal.\n\n**Best move:** Bxf3\n\n**Main line:** 1...Bxf3 2.Bxf3 (or 2.gxf3) Qxg5+ and Black has won the bishop.\n\n**Motif:** discoveredAttack (removing the Nf3 discovers that the Qa5 attacks Bg5)\n\n**Explanation (3-5 sentences):**\nWhen White played Bg5, the bishop blocked the queen's diagonal to the f3-knight. By capturing Bxf3, Black removes this piece, discovering an attack on the undefended Bg5. White must recapture the bishop, but both recaptures (Bxf3 or gxf3) leave the Bg5 undefended. Black then plays Qxg5, winning the bishop outright. The lesson: look for moves that remove pieces blocking your pieces' lines of attack\u2014you might discover a hanging target behind them.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bxf3\", \"line\": [\"Bxf3\", \"Bxf3\", \"Qxg5\"], \"motifs\": [\"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "a5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "e3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-s